Bluetooth character-device module for the native connectivity source build.

The open/close mutex protects the exclusive-open flag together with WMT power
transitions and callback registration. A second open waits for an in-progress
transition, then returns the existing -EIO error if another open succeeded.
Close releases ownership after callback removal and the function-off request.
Failed open/close paths release the mutex so a later open can retry.

From the kernel root, run the host concurrency regression with:

  python3 drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/source/common/test/test_bt_open.py

The test extracts BT_open/BT_close and the mutex declaration. Pthread gates
hold the first WMT power transition until a second caller reaches either the
mutex or the old overlapping WMT call. It checks simultaneous opens, open after
a failed first open, close/open overlap, existing-open rejection, transport
failures, and retry. Both dedicated-log configurations are compiled; log calls
use host stubs. No timing sleeps, module load, or hardware access is required.

Use --revision REF --case open-open or --case close-open to reproduce the old
interleavings. See ../../common/README for startup and WMT read regressions,
and ../../README.md for source integration and runtime dependencies.
